# ---- the game's own modes (item 165): each is a C++ singleton with a RUNNING byte of its own. Its start (the
# shared Mode_Shared::v[2] 0xa8ce4, or the mode's own for Escape Nimrod and Future Hurry Up) sets the object's
# byte +0x74 (Mode_Shared's +0x6c, the base at +8); its stop (the mode's v[3] -> Mode_Shared::v[1] 0xa8c90)
# and its completion check (Mode_Shared::v[5] 0xa8f2c) clear it. Instances from the calls of each class's
# own virtuals with r0 loaded (the dispatcher 0x9c9ec starts seven of them). Any byte set is one of its modes.
